1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:05,059
Imagine Priya. A bright student from a
small town in Andhra Pradesh.

2
00:00:05,109 --> 00:00:09,038
She understands logic, but every
coding class is in English,

3
00:00:09,088 --> 00:00:11,160
a language she doesn't think in.

4
00:00:11,260 --> 00:00:16,040
She is not alone. Every year, India
produces about 1.1 crore graduates.

5
00:00:16,140 --> 00:00:18,990
Only about half of them are
judged ready for a job.

6
00:00:19,090 --> 00:00:24,260
And graduates are four times more likely to
be jobless: 13 percent, against 3.

7
00:00:24,310 --> 00:00:26,000
2 percent for all workers.

8
00:00:26,100 --> 00:00:30,840
Only 1 in 10 Indians speak English. Yet
engineering is taught in English.

9
00:00:30,940 --> 00:00:35,800
44 percent of engineering students told AICTE
they want to learn in their mother

10
00:00:35,850 --> 00:00:36,230
tongue.

11
00:00:36,330 --> 00:00:40,990
What if Priya could learn in her own language,
and prove every skill she learns?

12
00:00:41,690 --> 00:00:46,871
Not a translated course. A teacher who speaks
the way she speaks: Telugu, Hindi,

13
00:00:46,921 --> 00:00:49,160
or the everyday Telugu-English mix.

14
00:00:49,260 --> 00:00:50,420
That's Qubirex.

15
00:00:51,520 --> 00:00:56,199
Professor Qubirex explains each idea, walks
through the code line by line,

16
00:00:56,249 --> 00:00:57,860
and answers her questions.

17
00:00:57,960 --> 00:01:00,425
She practises real code, with real tests,

18
00:01:00,475 --> 00:01:03,430
and a fresh check confirms she
can do it herself.

19
00:01:03,530 --> 00:01:07,135
Every skill she proves goes on a
signed Capability Passport.

20
00:01:07,185 --> 00:01:08,840
Anyone can verify it online.

21
00:01:08,940 --> 00:01:13,530
Colleges see who is ready and who needs
help. Employers hire on proof.

22
00:01:14,430 --> 00:01:19,990
Learn, practise, prove, and get seen by
employers. A to Z, in one place.

23
00:01:21,290 --> 00:01:27,797
Why now? Because IT fresher hiring has fallen
80% in three years, from 6 lakh to 1.

24
00:01:27,847 --> 00:01:28,350
2 lakh.

25
00:01:29,050 --> 00:01:32,333
A degree alone is no longer enough.
As Jensen Huang said:

26
00:01:32,383 --> 00:01:34,847
you're not going to lose
your job to an AI,

27
00:01:34,897 --> 00:01:38,180
but you're going to lose your job
to someone who uses AI.

28
00:01:38,280 --> 00:01:43,300
AI is like a recipe. It gives the steps, but
you still cook. AI writes code,

29
00:01:43,350 --> 00:01:47,370
but someone must check it. Why
shouldn't that someone be you?

30
00:01:48,470 --> 00:01:53,310
And 98 percent of India's internet users
already use Indian-language content.

31
00:01:53,410 --> 00:01:56,947
Other platforms already teach coding,
some in Indian languages.

32
00:01:56,997 --> 00:01:58,940
Qubirex is different in three ways.

33
00:02:00,540 --> 00:02:04,803
Qubirex gives proof of skills, one
journey from learning to hiring,

34
00:02:04,853 --> 00:02:06,670
and tools built for colleges.

35
00:02:06,770 --> 00:02:09,095
Next, a pilot with one partner college,

36
00:02:09,145 --> 00:02:12,200
to measure exactly how many more
students get jobs.

37
00:02:13,500 --> 00:02:18,497
Qubirex. Your language. Your
skills. Your future.
